From 76b377707c02a9bba2d30b7f4bb48a87cf7a70f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dave Stevenson <dave.stevenson@raspberrypi.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:39:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: ov5647: Grab [HV]FLIP controls when streaming

The HFLIP and VFLIP controls change the pixel format, so
can not be changed whilst streaming.

Grab those controls when starting streaming, and release
them when stopping.

Fixes: 743550826ba5 ("media: i2c: ov5647: Support HFLIP and VFLIP")
Signed-off-by: Dave Stevenson <dave.stevenson@raspberrypi.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/ov5647.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5647.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5647.c
@@ -816,6 +816,9 @@ static int ov5647_s_stream(struct v4l2_s
 		pm_runtime_put(&client->dev);
 	}
 
+	__v4l2_ctrl_grab(sensor->vflip, enable);
+	__v4l2_ctrl_grab(sensor->hflip, enable);
+
 	mutex_unlock(&sensor->lock);
 
 	return 0;
